    summary: "Brian Huntly is President Elect of the European Hematology Association and Professor of Leukaemia Stem Cell Biology at the University of Cambridge. His group investigates the transcriptional and epigenetic mechanisms that initiate and maintain acute myeloid leukaemia. He combines clinical haematology practice with laboratory research on novel leukaemia therapies.",
